{"text": "I need to reach the target number 24 using the numbers 9, 10, 10, and 13 exactly once each.", "start": 0, "end": 91, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I can use addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division.", "start": 92, "end": 154, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I should try different combinations.", "start": 155, "end": 191, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "First, since multiplication and division might give larger or smaller numbers quickly, I should consider those.", "start": 193, "end": 304, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Also, I have two 10s, which might be useful because multiplying by 10 is easy.", "start": 305, "end": 383, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me list the numbers: 9, 10, 10, 13.", "start": 385, "end": 424, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I need to get to 24.", "start": 426, "end": 446, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Maybe I can make something close to 24 and then adjust.", "start": 447, "end": 502, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, 13 + 10 is 23, which is close to 24.", "start": 504, "end": 553, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then I have 9 and another 10 left.", "start": 554, "end": 588, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But I need to use all numbers.", "start": 589, "end": 619, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So if I do 13 + 10 = 23, then I have to incorporate 9 and the other 10.", "start": 620, "end": 691, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Maybe (13 + 10) + (10 - 9) = 23 + 1 = 24.", "start": 692, "end": 733, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But that uses addition and subtraction, and I used each number once.", "start": 734, "end": 802, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me write it down.", "start": 803, "end": 824, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 + 10) + (10 - 9) = 23 + 1 = 24.", "start": 826, "end": 861, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "That seems to work.", "start": 862, "end": 881, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But is this using each number exactly once?", "start": 882, "end": 925, "label": "checkQuestion"}
{"text": "Yes: 13, 10, 10, and 9.", "start": 926, "end": 949, "label": "confirm"}
{"text": "Operations: +, +, and -.", "start": 950, "end": 974, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "The problem says \"use each number exactly once with +, -, *, /\", but it doesn't specify that I have to use all operations, just that I can use them.", "start": 976, "end": 1124, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So I think this is fine.", "start": 1125, "end": 1149, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But let me confirm: (13 + 10) is 23, then (10 - 9) is 1, then 23 + 1 = 24.", "start": 1151, "end": 1225, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perfect.", "start": 1226, "end": 1234, "label": "autoPositive"}
{"text": "I could write it as 13 + 10 + (10 - 9) = 13 + 10 + 1 = 24, same thing.", "start": 1236, "end": 1306, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Now, is there another way?", "start": 1308, "end": 1334, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "Maybe using multiplication or division.", "start": 1335, "end": 1374, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, 10 and 10 multiplied is 100, which is too big, then divided by something.", "start": 1376, "end": 1462, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "100 divided by something to get around 24.", "start": 1463, "end": 1505, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "100 / 4 = 25, which is close, but I don't have a 4.", "start": 1507, "end": 1558, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I have 9 and 13.", "start": 1559, "end": 1575, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 9 = 4, so (10 * 10) / (13 - 9) = 100 / 4 = 25.", "start": 1577, "end": 1628, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But 25 is not 24, it's one more.", "start": 1629, "end": 1661, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So close but not quite.", "start": 1662, "end": 1685, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then I need to subtract 1 or something, but I have no numbers left.", "start": 1687, "end": 1754, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "All numbers are used: two 10s for multiplication, 13 and 9 for subtraction.", "start": 1755, "end": 1830, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "In this case, I used both 10s in multiplication, and 13 and 9 in subtraction, so all used, but I got 25, not 24.", "start": 1832, "end": 1944, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So not quite.", "start": 1946, "end": 1959, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Maybe I can do something with 13 and 9 first.", "start": 1961, "end": 2006, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 9 = 4, then I have two 10s.", "start": 2008, "end": 2040, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 + 10 = 20, plus 4 is 24.", "start": 2041, "end": 2068, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But that would be (10 + 10) + (13 - 9) = 20 + 4 = 24.", "start": 2069, "end": 2122, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Similar to my first idea.", "start": 2123, "end": 2148, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "In fact, it's the same as before, just different grouping.", "start": 2150, "end": 2208, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "In my first one, I had 13 + 10 + (10 - 9), which is 13 + 10 + 1 = 24.", "start": 2210, "end": 2279, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Here, (10 + 10) + (13 - 9) = 20 + 4 = 24.", "start": 2281, "end": 2322, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So essentially the same thing.", "start": 2324, "end": 2354, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Now, can I use multiplication?", "start": 2356, "end": 2386, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "Suppose I do 13 * something.", "start": 2388, "end": 2416, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 2 = 26, too big.", "start": 2417, "end": 2438, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 1. something.", "start": 2439, "end": 2457, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Or division: 10 / something.", "start": 2459, "end": 2487, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another idea: 24 is 12 * 2, but I don't have 12 directly.", "start": 2489, "end": 2546, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 + 2, but no 2.", "start": 2548, "end": 2565, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 11, no.", "start": 2567, "end": 2579, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps (10 + 10) * something.", "start": 2581, "end": 2611, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "20 * 1.2 = 24, but I have 9 and 13, not sure.", "start": 2613, "end": 2658, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 9 = 4, then 10 + 10 = 20, but 20 * 1.2 isn't easy.", "start": 2660, "end": 2715, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Division: 24 / 1 = 24, but not helpful.", "start": 2717, "end": 2756, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 10 - 13) / something.", "start": 2758, "end": 2785, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 * 10 = 100, minus 13 is 87, then divide by something to get 24.", "start": 2787, "end": 2853, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "87 / 24 = 3.625, not integer, and I have 9 left, 87 / 9 is about 9.666, not 24.", "start": 2854, "end": 2933, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not good.", "start": 2935, "end": 2944, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 + 11) * something, but no 11.", "start": 2946, "end": 2979, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another thought: 10 and 10, I can make 100, or 1, or 0, etc.", "start": 2981, "end": 3041, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 / 10 = 1, then I have 9 and 13.", "start": 3043, "end": 3077, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 + 9 = 22, plus 1 is 23, not 24.", "start": 3079, "end": 3113, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 + 9 = 22, plus 10/10=1, 23.", "start": 3115, "end": 3145, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 + 11, but no.", "start": 3147, "end": 3163, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 * 10) / something.", "start": 3165, "end": 3187, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 10 = 130, divided by what?", "start": 3189, "end": 3220, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "130 / 5.416, not good.", "start": 3221, "end": 3243, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "With the other 10 and 9.", "start": 3245, "end": 3269, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "130 / (10 - 9/ something), messy.", "start": 3271, "end": 3304, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps subtraction: 10 * 13 = 130, minus something.", "start": 3306, "end": 3358, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "130 - 106 = 24, but 106 is not easy.", "start": 3360, "end": 3396, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 * 10 = 100, then 130 - 100 = 30, too big, and I have 9 left.", "start": 3398, "end": 3461, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not working.", "start": 3463, "end": 3475, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Division: 24 = 240 / 10, and I have another 10 and 9 and 13.", "start": 3477, "end": 3537, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "240 / 10 = 24, but how to get 240.", "start": 3539, "end": 3573, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "10 * 24, circular.", "start": 3575, "end": 3593, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 18.461, no.", "start": 3595, "end": 3611, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 * 26.666, no.", "start": 3613, "end": 3628, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 + 14) * something, but no 14.", "start": 3630, "end": 3663, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 + 11, no.", "start": 3665, "end": 3677, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another idea: 10 - (13 - 10) = 10 - 3 = 7, then I have 9 left.", "start": 3679, "end": 3741, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "7 and 9, 7 * 9 = 63, too big, or 9 - 7 = 2, not 24.", "start": 3742, "end": 3793, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not good.", "start": 3795, "end": 3804, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 10) / (10 / 2.4), messy.", "start": 3806, "end": 3836, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps I should consider fractions.", "start": 3838, "end": 3874, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, 13 - 10 = 3, then 10 / (3/ something), not clear.", "start": 3876, "end": 3938, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 divided by (13 - 10) is 10 / 3, about 3.333, then I have 9.", "start": 3940, "end": 4002, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 * 3.333 = 30, not 24.", "start": 4003, "end": 4026, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Or (10 / (13 - 10)) * something.", "start": 4028, "end": 4060, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 10 = 3, 10 / 3, then multiply by 9?", "start": 4062, "end": 4102, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 / 3) * 9 = 90/3 = 30, not 24.", "start": 4103, "end": 4136, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Divide by 9?", "start": 4138, "end": 4150, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "(10 / 3) / 9 = 10/27, small.", "start": 4151, "end": 4179, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not good.", "start": 4181, "end": 4190, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps with the other 10.", "start": 4192, "end": 4218, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another combination: let's use multiplication and addition.", "start": 4220, "end": 4279, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Suppose 9 * 3 = 27, close to 24, then subtract 3, but I need to make 3 with the other numbers.", "start": 4281, "end": 4375, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, 13 - 10 = 3, then 9 * 3 - 3, but I have two 3s?", "start": 4377, "end": 4437, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "No, 9 * (13 - 10) = 9 * 3 = 27, then I have another 10 left.", "start": 4438, "end": 4498, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "27 - 3 = 24, but I don't have another 3, I have a 10.", "start": 4499, "end": 4552, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "27 - 10 = 17, not 24.", "start": 4554, "end": 4575, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(9 * 3) - 3, but I need to make two 3s.", "start": 4577, "end": 4616, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "With 13 and 10, I can make one 3: 13 - 10 = 3.", "start": 4618, "end": 4664, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then with the other 10, how to make another 3?", "start": 4666, "end": 4712, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "10 - 7, no.", "start": 4713, "end": 4724, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not possible.", "start": 4726, "end": 4739, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 / (10/3) = 10 * 3/10 = 3, but that uses two 10s and I need a 3 from somewhere.", "start": 4741, "end": 4822, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Assume I have one 3 from 13-10, but I used 13 and one 10, then I have another 10 and 9.", "start": 4824, "end": 4911, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So if I do (13 - 10) = 3, then I have 10 and 9.", "start": 4913, "end": 4960, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I need to get to 24 with 3, 10, 9.", "start": 4962, "end": 4996, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 * 3 = 27, minus 3, but no extra 3.", "start": 4998, "end": 5034, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 + 9 + 3 = 22, not 24.", "start": 5036, "end": 5060, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 * 3 - 6, no 6.", "start": 5062, "end": 5079, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not working.", "start": 5081, "end": 5093, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps division: 24 = 48 / 2, but no 48 or 2.", "start": 5095, "end": 5141, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "12 * 2 = 24.", "start": 5143, "end": 5155, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "How to get 12 and 2.", "start": 5157, "end": 5177, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "For example, 10 + 2 = 12, but 2 from where?", "start": 5179, "end": 5222, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "13 - 11, no.", "start": 5223, "end": 5235, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 - 8, no.", "start": 5237, "end": 5248, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "With 9 and 13, 13 - 9 = 4, not 2.", "start": 5250, "end": 5283, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 + 10) / something = 20/ something.", "start": 5285, "end": 5323, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "20 / (5/6) = 20 * 6/5 = 24, but I need to make 5/6 with 9 and 13, not possible.", "start": 5325, "end": 5404, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 and 9, 13/9 is about 1.444, not 5/6.", "start": 5406, "end": 5445, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not good.", "start": 5447, "end": 5456, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another idea: (13 * 10 - 10) / something.", "start": 5458, "end": 5499, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 10 = 130, minus 10 = 120, then divide by 5 to get 24.", "start": 5501, "end": 5559, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "120 / 5 = 24.", "start": 5560, "end": 5573, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Now, do I have a 5?", "start": 5575, "end": 5594, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "I have 9 left.", "start": 5595, "end": 5609, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 - 4, no.", "start": 5610, "end": 5620, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "120 / 5, but 5 from where?", "start": 5622, "end": 5648, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "If I can make 5 with 9, but 9 - 4, no.", "start": 5650, "end": 5688, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 * 10 - 10) / (9 / 2.4), messy.", "start": 5690, "end": 5724, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not helpful.", "start": 5726, "end": 5738, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps I should consider the order of operations differently.", "start": 5740, "end": 5802, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me try to use the two 10s to make a fraction or something.", "start": 5804, "end": 5866, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 / 10 = 1, then I have 9 and 13.", "start": 5868, "end": 5902, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 + 9 = 22, 22 + 1 = 23, or 22 * 1 = 22, not 24.", "start": 5904, "end": 5953, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 9 = 117, too big, divided by 10 is 11.7, not 24.", "start": 5955, "end": 6008, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 * 9) / (10 / 10 * something), no.", "start": 6010, "end": 6047, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another thought: 24 = 30 - 6, and 30 is 3*10, 6 is 2*3, but complicated.", "start": 6049, "end": 6121, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 * 3 = 30, but 3 from 13-10, then I have another 10 and 9.", "start": 6123, "end": 6183, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So (13 - 10) * 10 = 3 * 10 = 30, then minus 6, but I have 9, 9 - 3, but 3 is already used.", "start": 6185, "end": 6275, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 - 10) * 10 - (10 - 4), no 4.", "start": 6277, "end": 6309, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "With 9, 30 - 6, but 6 not available.", "start": 6311, "end": 6347, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "30 - 9 + 3, but 3 is used, and +3 not.", "start": 6349, "end": 6387, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 - 10) * 10 - 9 + 3, but I can't reuse 3.", "start": 6389, "end": 6433, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not possible.", "start": 6435, "end": 6448, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps division: (10 * 10) / (13/3. something), no.", "start": 6450, "end": 6502, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's list all possible ways.", "start": 6504, "end": 6533, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Since I have two 10s, maybe I can do (10 - something) * something.", "start": 6535, "end": 6601, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 - x, then multiply by y.", "start": 6603, "end": 6630, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, 10 - 2 = 8, 8 * 3 = 24, but I need to make 2 and 3.", "start": 6632, "end": 6696, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 11, no.", "start": 6698, "end": 6710, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "With 9 and 13, 13 - 9 = 4, not 2.", "start": 6712, "end": 6745, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 + 14) * 1, no.", "start": 6747, "end": 6765, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another idea: 13 + 11 = 24, and 11 from 10 + 1, and 1 from 10/10.", "start": 6767, "end": 6832, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So 13 + (10 + (10/10))?", "start": 6834, "end": 6857, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's see: 10/10 = 1, then 10 + 1 = 11, then 13 + 11 = 24.", "start": 6858, "end": 6916, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But I used three 10s?", "start": 6918, "end": 6939, "label": "checkQuestion"}
{"text": "No: numbers: 13, 10, 10, and 10/10 uses two 10s for division?", "start": 6940, "end": 7001, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "No.", "start": 7002, "end": 7005, "label": "disagreement"}
{"text": "10/10 is one operation with two 10s, so it uses both 10s.", "start": 7007, "end": 7064, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then I have 13 and that result.", "start": 7066, "end": 7097, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "In expression: 13 + (10 + (10 / 10))", "start": 7099, "end": 7135, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Now, 10 / 10 = 1, then 10 + 1 = 11, then 13 + 11 = 24.", "start": 7137, "end": 7191, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But the numbers used: first 10/10 uses two 10s, then another 10 for the addition?", "start": 7193, "end": 7274, "label": "checkQuestion"}
{"text": "No.", "start": 7275, "end": 7278, "label": "disagreement"}
{"text": "In the expression: 13 + (10 + (10 / 10))", "start": 7280, "end": 7320, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "The innermost is 10 / 10, which is two 10s.", "start": 7322, "end": 7365, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then that result is added to another 10?", "start": 7367, "end": 7407, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "10 + (result of 10/10), so that's a different 10.", "start": 7408, "end": 7457, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's count the numbers: there are three 10s here?", "start": 7459, "end": 7509, "label": "checkQuestion"}
{"text": "No.", "start": 7510, "end": 7513, "label": "disagreement"}
{"text": "In the expression: 13 + (10 + (10 / 10))", "start": 7515, "end": 7555, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "The numbers are: one 13, and three 10s?", "start": 7557, "end": 7596, "label": "checkQuestion"}
{"text": "No: the first 10 in (10 + ...) is one 10, and the (10 / 10) has two more 10s, so three 10s, but I only have two 10s available.", "start": 7597, "end": 7723, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I think I confused myself.", "start": 7725, "end": 7751, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I have only two 10s: let's say 10a and 10b.", "start": 7753, "end": 7796, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "In the expression: 13 + (10a + (10b / 10?)) but I don't have a third 10.", "start": 7798, "end": 7870, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10b / 10? I only have two 10s.", "start": 7872, "end": 7902, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So if I do 10 / 10, that uses both 10s for division, giving 1.", "start": 7904, "end": 7966, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then I have 13 and that 1, and I need to use the other number, which is 9?", "start": 7968, "end": 8042, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "No, all numbers are used in the expression.", "start": 8043, "end": 8086, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "In 13 + (10 + (10 / 10)), the (10 / 10) uses two 10s, but then there is another 10 in (10 + ...), so that's a third 10, which I don't have.", "start": 8088, "end": 8227, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So invalid.", "start": 8229, "end": 8240, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "To write it properly, I need to use each number once, so I can't reuse a number.", "start": 8242, "end": 8322, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So in this case, for (10 / 10), it consumes two 10s, output is 1.", "start": 8324, "end": 8389, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then I have 13 and 9 left, and I need to combine with 1.", "start": 8391, "end": 8447, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 + 9 + 1 = 23, not 24.", "start": 8449, "end": 8473, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 1 + 9 = 22, etc., not 24.", "start": 8475, "end": 8505, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So not.", "start": 8507, "end": 8514, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Back to my first solution, which seems correct.", "start": 8516, "end": 8563, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But let me see if there's a way with multiplication or division to make it interesting.", "start": 9343, "end": 9430, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Suppose I do 10 * (13 - 9) * something.", "start": 9432, "end": 9471, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 9 = 4, 10 * 4 = 40, then I have another 10.", "start": 9473, "end": 9521, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "40 / 10 * something, 40/10=4, not 24.", "start": 9522, "end": 9559, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * (13 - 9)) / 10 * 6, no.", "start": 9561, "end": 9590, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not.", "start": 9592, "end": 9596, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 * (13 - 9) - 16, no.", "start": 9598, "end": 9621, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps (10 + 14) * 1, but 14 from 10 + 4, 4 from 13-9, so (10 + (13 - 9)) * (10 / 10) = (10 + 4) * 1 = 14 * 1 = 14, not 24.", "start": 9623, "end": 9747, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 + (13 - 9)) * 10 / 10, same thing.", "start": 9749, "end": 9787, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not.", "start": 9789, "end": 9793, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 10) / (5/1.2), no.", "start": 9795, "end": 9819, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I think I should conclude that the simplest way is with addition and subtraction.", "start": 9821, "end": 9902, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But in my first solution, I used addition and subtraction, no multiplication or division.", "start": 9904, "end": 9993, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But the problem allows them, but doesn't require.", "start": 9995, "end": 10044, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps there is a way with division.", "start": 10046, "end": 10083, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, 240 / 10 = 24, and 240 from 24 * 10, circular.", "start": 10085, "end": 10144, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 18.461, no.", "start": 10146, "end": 10162, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 * 26.666, no.", "start": 10164, "end": 10179, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 * 10 * 10) / something, 1300 / 54.166, no.", "start": 10181, "end": 10227, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1300 / 54.166 is about 24, but not exact.", "start": 10229, "end": 10270, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "With 9, 1300 / 9 = 144.444, too big.", "start": 10272, "end": 10308, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 * 10) + (10 * 1.4), no.", "start": 10310, "end": 10337, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another idea: (10 - 9/10) * something, but 9/10 = 0.9, 10 - 0.9 = 9.1, not helpful.", "start": 8661, "end": 8744, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 * 2) - 2, but 26-2=24, and 2 from 10/5, no.", "start": 8746, "end": 8793, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 2 = 26, but 2 from 10/5, no 5.", "start": 8795, "end": 8830, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "With 10 and 10, 10/10=1, not 2.", "start": 8832, "end": 8863, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 + 10) * 1.2, but 1.2 from 12/10, circular.", "start": 8865, "end": 8911, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I think I'm stuck.", "start": 8913, "end": 8931, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps division: 48 / 2 = 24.", "start": 8933, "end": 8963, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "48 from 10 * 4.8, no.", "start": 8965, "end": 8986, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 3.692, no.", "start": 8988, "end": 9003, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 10) - 76, no.", "start": 9005, "end": 9024, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not working.", "start": 9026, "end": 9038, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 + 11) but no 11.", "start": 9040, "end": 9060, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 * 13 = 130, 130 - 106 = 24, 106 from 10*10.6, no.", "start": 9062, "end": 9114, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps with subtraction and division.", "start": 9116, "end": 9154, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another thought: 9 * (10 / (10 / 4)) but 10/4=2.5, 10/2.5=4, then 9*4=36, not 24.", "start": 9156, "end": 9237, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not good.", "start": 9239, "end": 9248, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 13 - 10) / (9 / 2.4), messy.", "start": 9250, "end": 9284, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I think I should accept that my first solution is fine.", "start": 9286, "end": 9341, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But let me see if there's a way with multiplication or division to make it interesting.", "start": 9343, "end": 9430, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Suppose I do 10 * (13 - 9) * something.", "start": 9432, "end": 9471, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 9 = 4, 10 * 4 = 40, then I have another 10.", "start": 9473, "end": 9521, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "40 / 10 * something, 40/10=4, not 24.", "start": 9522, "end": 9559, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * (13 - 9)) / 10 * 6, no.", "start": 9561, "end": 9590, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not.", "start": 9592, "end": 9596, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 * (13 - 9) - 16, no.", "start": 9598, "end": 9621, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps (10 + 14) * 1, but 14 from 10 + 4, 4 from 13-9, so (10 + (13 - 9)) * (10 / 10) = (10 + 4) * 1 = 14 * 1 = 14, not 24.", "start": 9623, "end": 9747, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 + (13 - 9)) * 10 / 10, same thing.", "start": 9749, "end": 9787, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not.", "start": 9789, "end": 9793, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 10) / (5/1.2), no.", "start": 9795, "end": 9819, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I think I should conclude that the simplest way is with addition and subtraction.", "start": 9821, "end": 9902, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But in my first solution, I used addition and subtraction, no multiplication or division.", "start": 9904, "end": 9993, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But the problem allows them, but doesn't require.", "start": 9995, "end": 10044, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps there is a way with division.", "start": 10046, "end": 10083, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, 240 / 10 = 24, and 240 from 24 * 10, circular.", "start": 10085, "end": 10144, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 18.461, no.", "start": 10146, "end": 10162, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 * 26.666, no.", "start": 10164, "end": 10179, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 * 10 * 10) / something, 1300 / 54.166, no.", "start": 10181, "end": 10227, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "1300 / 54.166 is about 24, but not exact.", "start": 10229, "end": 10270, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "With 9, 1300 / 9 = 144.444, too big.", "start": 10272, "end": 10308, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 * 10) + (10 * 1.4), no.", "start": 10310, "end": 10337, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another idea: (10 - 9/10) * something, but 9/10 = 0.9, 10 - 0.9 = 9.1, not helpful.", "start": 8661, "end": 8744, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 * 2) - 2, but 26-2=24, and 2 from 10/5, no.", "start": 8746, "end": 8793, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 2 = 26, but 2 from 10/5, no 5.", "start": 8795, "end": 8830, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "With 10 and 10, 10/10=1, not 2.", "start": 8832, "end": 8863, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 + 10) * 1.2, but 1.2 from 12/10, circular.", "start": 8865, "end": 8911, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I think I'm stuck.", "start": 8913, "end": 8931, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps division: 48 / 2 = 24.", "start": 8933, "end": 8963, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "48 from 10 * 4.8, no.", "start": 8965, "end": 8986, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 * 3.692, no.", "start": 8988, "end": 9003, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 10) - 76, no.", "start": 9005, "end": 9024, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not working.", "start": 9026, "end": 9038, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 + 11) but no 11.", "start": 9040, "end": 9060, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 * 13 = 130, 130 - 106 = 24, 106 from 10*10.6, no.", "start": 9062, "end": 9114, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps with subtraction and division.", "start": 9116, "end": 9154, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another thought: 9 * (10 / (10 / 4)) but 10/4=2.5, 10/2.5=4, then 9*4=36, not 24.", "start": 9156, "end": 9237, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not good.", "start": 9239, "end": 9248, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 13 - 10) / (9 / 2.4), messy.", "start": 9250, "end": 9284, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I think I should accept that my first solution is fine.", "start": 9286, "end": 9341, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But let me think about the order.", "start": 11773, "end": 11806, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Another common way: 10 * (3 - 0. something), but not.", "start": 11808, "end": 11861, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 - (13 - 10)) * 12, no.", "start": 11863, "end": 11889, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "13 - 10 = 3, 10 - 3 = 7, then 7 and 9, 7*9=63, or 9-7=2, not 24.", "start": 11891, "end": 11955, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 13) / 5.416, no.", "start": 11957, "end": 11979, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps I can use the numbers in a fraction.", "start": 11981, "end": 12025, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, (10 × 10 × 24/ something), but circular.", "start": 12027, "end": 12080, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 × 24/10), but 24 not available.", "start": 12082, "end": 12117, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not helpful.", "start": 12119, "end": 12131, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I recall that 24 can be made from 8 * 3, or 6 * 4, etc.", "start": 12133, "end": 12188, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "8 from 10 - 2, but no 2.", "start": 12190, "end": 12214, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "6 from 10 - 4, no.", "start": 12216, "end": 12234, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "4 from 13 - 9, as before.", "start": 12236, "end": 12261, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then with two 10s, I can do 10 + 10 + 4 = 24, as before.", "start": 12263, "end": 12319, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Or 10 * 2.4, but 2.4 from 12/5, no.", "start": 12321, "end": 12356, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 13 - 10) / 5, but 120 / 5 = 24, and 5 from where?", "start": 12358, "end": 12413, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "If I had a 5, but I have 9.", "start": 12414, "end": 12441, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 - 4, but no 4.", "start": 12443, "end": 12459, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 * 13 - 10) / (9 / 2.4), but 2.4 not available.", "start": 12461, "end": 12511, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Unless I make 2.4 from numbers, but I have no other.", "start": 12513, "end": 12565, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "I think it's not possible, so my initial solution is best.", "start": 12567, "end": 12625, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perhaps (9 - 10/10) * something, 10/10=1, 9-1=8, then 8 * 3 = 24, but 3 from 13-10, so (9 - 10/10) * (13 - 10)", "start": 12627, "end": 12737, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Now, let's see: first, 10/10 = 1, using two 10s.", "start": 12739, "end": 12787, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 9 - 1 = 8", "start": 12789, "end": 12803, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then 13 - 10? But I used both 10s already?", "start": 12805, "end": 12847, "label": "checkQuestion"}
{"text": "No.", "start": 12848, "end": 12851, "label": "disagreement"}
{"text": "In the expression: (9 - (10 / 10)) * (13 - 10)", "start": 12853, "end": 12899, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But (13 - 10), the 10 here is the same as in the division?", "start": 12901, "end": 12959, "label": "checkQuestion"}
{"text": "No, I have only two 10s.", "start": 12960, "end": 12984, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's specify: let the numbers be 10a and 10b.", "start": 12986, "end": 13032, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So (9 - (10a / 10b)) * (13 - 10?) but I don't have another 10.", "start": 13034, "end": 13096, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "In (9 - (10a / 10b)), that uses 9, 10a, 10b.", "start": 13129, "end": 13173, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Then I have 13 left, not used.", "start": 13175, "end": 13205, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So I need to incorporate 13.", "start": 13207, "end": 13235, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "The expression is (9 - (10/10)) * something with 13, but what?", "start": -1, "end": -1, "label": "setQuestion"}
{"text": "Multiply by 3, but 3 not available.", "start": 13400, "end": 13435, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(9 - (10/10)) * 13 / something, but 8 * 13 = 104, divided by 4.333, not good.", "start": 13437, "end": 13514, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not working.", "start": 13516, "end": 13528, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Therefore, I think the only reasonable way is the first one I found.", "start": 13530, "end": 13598, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So, to write it clearly: (13 + 10) + (10 - 9) = 23 + 1 = 24", "start": 13600, "end": 13659, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Or with different grouping: 10 + 10 + 13 - 9, since 10 + 10 = 20, +13 = 33, minus 9 is 24?", "start": 13661, "end": 13751, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "20 + 13 = 33, 33 - 9 = 24.", "start": 13752, "end": 13778, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Oh, that's better.", "start": 13779, "end": 13797, "label": "autoPositive"}
{"text": "10 + 10 + 13 - 9 = 20 + 13 = 33, minus 9 is 24.", "start": 13799, "end": 13846, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Yes, and it uses all numbers: two 10s, one 13, one 9.", "start": 13848, "end": 13901, "label": "confirm"}
{"text": "Operations: +, +, -.", "start": 13903, "end": 13923, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Perfect.", "start": 13925, "end": 13933, "label": "autoPositive"}
{"text": "And it's simple.", "start": 13935, "end": 13951, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "10 + 13 + 10 - 9, same thing.", "start": 13953, "end": 13982, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So, I think that's the answer.", "start": 13984, "end": 14014, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But the problem says \"use each number exactly once with +, -, *, /\", and in this case, I used + and -, no * or /, but it should be fine.", "start": 14016, "end": 14152, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "If I must use multiplication or division, I can probably find a way, but it doesn't say I must, so it's acceptable.", "start": 14154, "end": 14269, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "For example, another way: (10 * 10 - 76) / something, no.", "start": 14271, "end": 14328, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(13 - 9) * (10 - 10/5), but no 5.", "start": 14330, "end": 14363, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Not possible.", "start": 14365, "end": 14378, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So, I'll go with that.", "start": 14380, "end": 14402, "label": "inform"}
